        "y0": 0.725148430978409,
        "x1": 0.8788241716771344,
        "y1": 0.7377275216459024
      },
      "text": "is the vector field governing the system, can we reconstruct f from the observed data ?",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.14215671314912684,
        "y0": 0.7401480518206202,
        "x1": 0.8825462191712623,
        "y1": 0.7527271424881136
      },
      "text": "This question has recently garnered significant interest among the machine learning and statistical com-",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11764690922755822,
        "y0": 0.7552995669721353,
        "x1": 0.18235083187327666,
        "y1": 0.7678786576396287
      },
      "text": "munities.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.19489960265315437,
        "y0": 0.7552995669721353,
        "x1": 0.5386272629881217,
        "y1": 0.7678786576396287
      },
      "text": "Most existing works focus on the case where f",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5474506452971813,
        "y0": 0.7552995669721353,
        "x1": 0.8823510462941687,
        "y1": 0.7678786576396287
      },
      "text": "is assumed to belong to a parametric class of",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
