        "y0": 0.7704510821236504,
        "x1": 0.8825482137842116,
        "y1": 0.7830301727911438
      },
      "text": "functions (e.g. see the surveys McGoff et al., 2015; Ramsay and Hooker, 2017; Dattner, 2021). In contrast,",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11764705882352941,
        "y0": 0.7854513387487392,
        "x1": 0.8823523427925858,
        "y1": 0.7980304294162326
      },
      "text": "the non-parametric literature is scarcer and primarily numerical (Chen et al., 2018; Heinonen et al., 2018;",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11764705882352941,
        "y0": 0.8006027190372197,
        "x1": 0.5982346877553104,
        "y1": 0.8131818097047132
      },
      "text": "Bhat et al., 2020; Gottwald and Reich, 2021; Lahouel et al., 2024).",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6084305009031608,
        "y0": 0.8006027190372197,
        "x1": 0.8825468175551471,
        "y1": 0.8131818097047132
      },
      "text": "More recently, some studies have pro-",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11764705882352941,
        "y0": 0.8157542341887349,
        "x1": 0.8117621926700368,
        "y1": 0.8283333248562283
      },
      "text": "vided theoretical analyses of the statistical performance of their proposed estimation strategies.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.8221544253280739,
        "y0": 0.8157542341887349,
        "x1": 0.8823495503344567,
        "y1": 0.8283333248562283
      },
      "text": "Notably,",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11764705882352941,
        "y0": 0.8307542403539022,
        "x1": 0.6425456128089256,
        "y1": 0.8433333310213956
      },
      "text": "Sch¨otz and Siebel (2024); Sch¨otz (2025) introduce two statistical models:",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6511729620640574,
        "y0": 0.8307542403539022,
        "x1": 0.8823521433312909,
        "y1": 0.8433333310213956
      },
      "text": "the snake model and the stubble",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11764790653403288,
        "y0": 0.8459057555054174,
        "x1": 0.8823524425232333,
        "y1": 0.8584848461729108
      },
      "text": "model. In the snake model, a few long trajectories are observed, covering the space of interest. In the stubble",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
